<</A<</BBox[249.449999 98.989999 385.47 603.779999]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>/Alt(Flow chart illustrating the biochemical pathway from glucose to L-lysine. The process begins with glucose, converting through several intermediates such as phosphoenolpyruvate \(PEP\), oxaloacetate \(OAA\), and aspartate. Key enzymes like aspartate kinase\ and dihydrodipicolinate synthase facilitate these conversions. The pathway continues through compounds like aspartate-semialdehyde and dihydrodipicolinate, eventually leading to L-lysine. Each step is connected by arrows, indicating the sequence of react\ions.)/K 1/P 9490 0 R/Pg 1097 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj9511 0 obj<</A<</BBox[89.799999 98.989999 349.68 603.779999]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>/Alt(Flow chart illustrating a biochemical pathway starting with glucose. It progresses through several steps involving compounds and enzymes: phosphoenolpyruvate, erythrose-4-phosphate, DAHP synthase, 3-deoxy-D-arabino-heptulosonate 7-phosphate, DHQ synthase,\ dehydroquinate, DHQ dehydratase, dehydroshikimate, shikimate dehydrogenase, shikimate, EPSP synthase, 5-enolpyruvylshikimate-3-phosphate, chorismate synthase, and ending with chorismate. Some text includes 'Unsupported markdown: escape' indicating format\ting issues.)/K 0/P 9490 0 R/Pg 1101 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj9512 0 obj<</K 1/P 9490 0 R/Pg 1101 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj9513 0 obj<</K 5/P 9490 0 R/Pg 1105 0 R/S/H2/Type/StructElem>>endobj9514 0 obj<</K[6 10922 0 R 8 10923 0 R 10 10924 0 R 12]/P 9490 0 R/Pg 1105 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj9515 0 obj<</K[13 10913 0 R 15 10914 0 R 17 10915 0 R 19]/P 9490 0 R/Pg 1105 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj9516 0 obj<</K 0/P 9490 0 R/Pg 1108 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj9517 0 obj<</K[1 10907 0 R 3 10908 0 R 5]/P 9490 0 R/Pg 1108 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj9518 0 obj<</K[6 10895 0 R 8 10896 0 R 10 10897 0 R 12 10898 0 R 14]/P 9490 0 R/Pg 1108 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endo